---
// Pricing (site-prelaunch.md §3) — copy verbatim from "Page: Pricing" (#41, FINAL).
// Monthly-only: no annual figures landed, so the designed billing toggle ships dormant
// (NOT built — zero JS, per the design's own conditional + PM annual-pricing decision).
// Connection-optional: works with or without a broker connection. Core's $49 is the
// Accepted price (pricing-artifact.md §1, human sign-off 2026-06-30), matching
// FastSpring's catalog exactly. No card CTA in #39 — no checkout exists. Tier symmetry
// is a compliance feature (spec §6.2): never differentiate.
// Free card (2026-07-22, stock-analyst-platform#1307): shipped decoupled from the
// trial-launch reveal (consult 0182, ADR 0145 item 6) — Free needs neither ORATS (#97)
// nor a live checkout, so it ships alone. The chooser block and Core's trial CTA stay
// gated on #97/#31 and are NOT part of this change.
// Trimmed from the #1307 canonical draft (human direction 2026-07-22): dropped
// "— ongoing, not a trial" and the standalone "No card required" line as redundant
// on a card with no CTA/checkout to contrast against. "Any ticker" → "any US-listed
// ticker" per consult 0416 (PM ruling): the product is US-only by design (ADR
// 0027/0028) and US-venue-scoped by construction; inline qualifier, not a footnote,
// to preserve tier-card symmetry (spec §6.2).
// Premium card removed (2026-08-02, stock-analyst-platform#1766/#1767): realizes
// pricing-artifact.md's go-live gate (human direction, 2026-07-22) — while #1304
// (live analyst research) is open, Premium is held out of checkout/pricing entirely
// (hidden, not offered), matching the in-app Plans page's Free/Core state. Re-add
// trigger: when #1304 and the deferred-layers.lit flip both close, re-add as its own
// copy PR (content preserved in site-copy-twiceover.md's git history pre-2026-08-02).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Offer JSON-LD (SEO audit 2026-07 finding 7) — the Accepted prices, verbatim from
// pricing-artifact.md §1 (human sign-off 2026-06-30). No numbers invented here.
// Premium omitted (#1766/#1767) — the go-live gate holds it out of pricing entirely;
// a structured-data Offer is as much an advertisement of it as the visible card.
const productJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Product",
  name: "TwiceOver",
  url: "https://twiceover.io/pricing/",
  offers: [
    { "@type": "Offer", name: "Free", price: "0", priceCurrency: "USD" },
    { "@type": "Offer", name: "Core", price: "49", priceCurrency: "USD" },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="Pricing — TwiceOver"
  description="One simple monthly subscription. No per-analysis charges. Use it with or without a broker connection."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(productJsonLd)} />
  <div class="page-title-block">
    <h1 class="type-heading-1">Simple subscription. You hold the decisions; we do the math.</h1>
    <p class="sub">One simple monthly subscription. No per-analysis charges. Use it with or without a broker connection — connecting read-only unlocks reads of your own positions against your own rules.</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="tier-grid">
    <li class="tier">
      <h2 class="type-heading-2">Free</h2>
      <p class="price type-display">$0</p>
      <ul>
        <li>15 reads a month</li>
        <li>The synthesis read on any US-listed ticker</li>
        <li>Key technical levels (basic), SEC/EDGAR fundamentals, macro regime context</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="tier">
      <h2 class="type-heading-2">Core</h2>
      <p class="price type-display">$49<span class="per">/mo</span></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read-only broker connection</li>
        <li>Held-position reads and new-idea reads</li>
        <li>Options math &amp; structure engine (breakevens, max profit/loss, collateral, P&amp;L)</li>
        <li>Your own rules, evaluated on live data</li>
        <li>Macro/regime context and the research layer</li>
        <li>Licensed market and options data</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="mor-line">Subscriptions are sold by <strong>Dodo Payments</strong>, our merchant of record; TwiceOver is the software and service you're using. Prices in USD. You can cancel anytime; see the <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.</p>
</Base>
